# Runtime TLS certificates & keys
# SEC-002: private key material must NEVER be committed. Operators stage
# certificates locally at deploy time; the binary generates an ephemeral
# in-memory authority when none are provisioned.
src-tauri/certs/*.crt
src-tauri/certs/*.key
src-tauri/certs/*.pem
src-tauri/certs/production.crt
src-tauri/certs/production.key

# Archived Historical Documentation
docs/archive/
docs/archive/*

# Release build bundles (large binaries) — never tracked
# Payloads are staged under release-artifacts/iyou_home_<VERSION>/ (outside
# dist/, which Vite's emptyOutDir wipes). The entire tree is ignored, including
# the flat manifests (MIRRORS.txt, SHA256SUMS*.txt): those are per-release build
# outputs regenerated by scripts/release.sh, not sources, and a stale checksum
# manifest committed to git is worse than no manifest at all.
#
# Mirror clients do NOT read these files from the repo. download_modal.js parses
# `release.body` off GitHub's CORS-friendly `releases/latest` endpoint, so
# scripts/release.sh embeds the magnet/IPFS metadata directly in the release
# body — that is the discovery surface, and it cannot depend on a tracked file.
release-artifacts/
